Z||000003||mwbackus||09-24-1999||06:04 AM||||Although it is not explicitly stated, in most cases, the advice that we offer assumes that one will use the directions in the manual as their primary tool for accomplishing tasks such as this.  Most of the information offered is more related to helpful shortcuts or observed trouble areas that solutions have been found for.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000004||dans87gt||09-24-1999||07:26 AM||||I have never had to loosen my bracket, only the top, bottom bolts, and the wiring||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||09-24-1999||10:34 AM||||I have an 85SE 2m6 4spd and have changed the altenator a couple of times.  There is the long pivot bolt on top which the altenator hangs from and there is a short bolt at the bottom belt tension adjusting bracket that threads into the altenator housing boss.  I've never had to loosen the altenator bracket.  Just remember to disconnect the battery cable first or you could be in for a nasty surprise when you are levering the unit out.||||reg||1
